    <description><![CDATA[<p><b>Time fetched:</b> Oct 7, 2026 7:30AM EDT</p><h2>LIVE OVATION AURORA FORECAST</h2><p><b>Gradient key</b><br><img src="https://wyattleathorn7.github.io/great-lakes-live-environment/aurora/legend.png" width="600" alt="gradient key"><br>OVATION auroral intensity, FIXED absolute scale 0&ndash;30+: <b>LOWEST 0</b> (transparent, no activity) &rarr; <b>6 bright green</b> (auroral oval overhead) &rarr; <b>14 orange</b> &rarr; <b>23 magenta</b> (severe) &rarr; <b>HIGHEST+ 30+</b> (violet extreme). Same intensity always shows the same color. Model-derived viewline in basin: <b>~63°N (north of this map — oval is poleward of the Great Lakes now)</b> (southernmost latitude reaching intensity 5+: aurora may be visible low on the northern horizon from there under dark, clear skies).</p><p>This entry auto-refreshes from the live overlay (source: NOAA/SWPC OVATION Prime aurora model (Aurora Viewline product family)).</p><p>Turn on/off independently of all other layers. Add this file once; new source cycles appear automatically.</p><p><i>Not endorsed by NOAA.</i></p>]]></description>
